SET description = 'Behavioural interview. Use only what was said in the conversation or notes. Never invent statements, numbers, employers or outcomes. If a topic was not discussed, write Not discussed; that is not evidence against the candidate. A claim the candidate makes without supporting detail, such as saying they are an excellent problem solver, is a self-claim, not verified evidence; label it as a self-claim. Keep contradictory statements visible instead of resolving them. If the transcript is short or unclear, say the evidence is thin. Do not score the candidate or give a hire or no-hire verdict. A section with little content can be a single line.'
WHERE id = 'default-behavioural-interview';
